{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc | sed -n '125,490p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc | sed -n '45,175p'; nl -ba src/cljc/dao/star/signals.cljc | head -24; rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\(deftest' test/dao/star/r4_test.clj\"","aggregated_output":"   125\t(defn- end\n   126\t  [x]\n   127\t  {:http/exchange x :http/effect :http/end})\n   128\t\n   129\t\n   130\t(defn- answer!\n   131\t  \"Head, one SSE projection, end: the reply to a one-shot exchange.\"\n   132\t  [config x occurrence model]\n   133\t  (emit! config [(head x \"text/event-stream\")\n   134\t                 (chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))\n   135\t                 (end x)]))\n   136\t\n   137\t\n   138\t(defn- patch!\n   139\t  \"Patch every open subscription whose exchange holder is holding.  The caller\n   140\t   has observed the holders' state for this pass and checked the lineage's.\"\n   141\t  [config s]\n   142\t  (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest s)]\n   143\t    (doseq [[x a] (:subs s)\n   144\t            :when (and (not (contains? (:sub-staged s) x))\n   145\t                       (lease/holding? a))]\n   146\t      (emit! config [(chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))]))))\n   147\t\n   148\t\n   149\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   150\t;; Session construction\n   151\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- decl\n   154\t  [capacity attribution]\n   155\t  (lease/medium-declaration capacity attribution))\n   156\t\n   157\t\n   158\t(defn- lineage-agent-config\n   159\t  [{:keys [tick lineage-lease facts units lineage-renewal-interval lease-capacity\n   160\t           facts-declaration]} s]\n   161\t  (let [subject {:dao.star/lineage s}]\n   162\t    {:self subject :grantor lease/lineage-grantor :subject subject\n   163\t     :units units :renewal-interval lineage-renewal-interval\n   164\t     :resolver lease/resolver :resolver-bindings lease/resolver-bindings\n   165\t     :tick tick\n   166\t     :fact {:handle lineage-lease :source lease/lineage-lease-source\n   167\t            :medium (decl lease-capacity :per-author-media)}\n   168\t     :writer {:handle facts :medium (assoc facts-declaration :attribution :envelope-key)}\n   169\t     :envelope {:dao.star/lineage s}}))\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\t(defn- exchange-agent-config\n   173\t  [{:keys [tick exchange-lease egress units exchange-renewal-interval lease-capacity]} x]\n   174\t  {:self :egress :grantor lease/exchange-grantor :subject {:http/exchange x}\n   175\t   :units units :renewal-interval exchange-renewal-interval\n   176\t   :resolver lease/resolver :resolver-bindings lease/resolver-bindings\n   177\t   :tick tick\n   178\t   :fact {:handle exchange-lease :source lease/exchange-lease-source\n   179\t          :medium (decl lease-capacity :per-author-media)}\n   180\t   :writer {:handle egress :medium (decl lease-capacity :per-author-media)}})\n   181\t\n   182\t\n   183\t(defn- last-model\n   184\t  \"Drain the view medium: the newest model emitted, the advanced cursor, and\n   185\t   whether the cursor answered a gap.\"\n   186\t  [handle cursor]\n   187\t  (let [r (lease/drain handle cursor)]\n   188\t    {:cursor (:cursor r) :model (last (:values r)) :emitted? (seq (:values r))\n   189\t     :gap? (:gap? r)}))\n   190\t\n   191\t\n   192\t(defn- update-session!\n   193\t  [driver s f & args]\n   194\t  (swap! driver (fn [d] (if (contains? (:sessions d) s)\n   195\t                          (apply update-in d [:sessions s] f args)\n   196\t                          d))))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(defn- forget!\n   200\t  \"A gap on a medium the session reads: forget every subscription and renew\n   201\t   nothing from then on.  The lineage's holder is marked gapped, so it renews\n   202\t   no lease; the leases lapse by silence.\"\n   203\t  [driver s]\n   204\t  (when-let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   205\t    (swap! (:agent sess) assoc :gapped? true)\n   206\t    (update-session! driver s assoc :subs {} :sub-staged #{})))\n   207\t\n   208\t\n   209\t(defn- begin!\n   210\t  \"Begin a lineage for exchange `x`: a fresh session with its own VM, the root\n   211\t   fact appended before anything is answered.  The begin page itself is staged\n   212\t   until the lineage grant has been observed (`flush-begin!`).  A root fact that\n   213\t   is not accepted starts nothing and answers nothing; the exchange lapses by\n   214\t   silence.\"\n   215\t  [driver x]\n   216\t  (let [{:keys [program facts] :as config} (:config @driver)\n   217\t        s (str (random-uuid))\n   218\t        in (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   219\t        out (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   220\t        medium (new-ring (:session-capacity config))\n   221\t        result (await/run (update program :env merge {'in in 'out out}))\n   222\t        {:keys [cursor model]} (last-model out (lease/oldest-cursor out))]\n   223\t    (when (ok? (stream/append! facts (facts/root s)))\n   224\t      (swap! driver assoc-in [:sessions s]\n   225\t             {:lineage s :medium medium :cursor (lease/oldest-cursor medium)\n   226\t              :vm-in in :vm-out out :out-cursor cursor :result result\n   227\t              :latest {:occurrence s :model model} :subs {} :sub-staged #{}\n   228\t              :begin-pending x\n   229\t              :agent (lease/make-agent (lineage-agent-config config s))}))))\n   230\t\n   231\t\n   232\t(defn begin-step!\n   233\t  \"Read the begin medium to `blocked`, beginning a lineage per message.  A gap\n   234\t   on it loses begin requests; every session forgets its subscriptions.\"\n   235\t  [driver]\n   236\t  (let [{:keys [config begin-cursor]} @driver\n   237\t        r (lease/drain (:begin config) begin-cursor)]\n   238\t    (swap! driver assoc :begin-cursor (:cursor r))\n   239\t    (when (:gap? r)\n   240\t      (doseq [s (sessions driver)] (forget! driver s)))\n   241\t    (doseq [m (:values r)\n   242\t            :when (and (map? m) (= :begin (:kind m)) (:exchange m))]\n   243\t      (begin! driver (:exchange m)))\n   244\t    driver))\n   245\t\n   246\t\n   247\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   248\t;; One session\n   249\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   250\t\n   251\t(defn- flush-begin!\n   252\t  \"Answer the staged begin page once the lineage grant is observed and the\n   253\t   holder is holding; drop it if the lease is already past its bound.\"\n   254\t  [driver s]\n   255\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   256\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   257\t        x (:begin-pending sess)]\n   258\t    (when x\n   259\t      (cond\n   260\t        (lease/past-bound? (:agent sess)) (update-session! driver s dissoc :begin-pending)\n   261\t        (lease/holding? (:agent sess))\n   262\t        (do (update-session! driver s dissoc :begin-pending)\n   263\t            (emit! config [(head x \"text/html\")\n   264\t                           (chunk-fx x ((:begin-fn config) s))\n   265\t                           (end x)]))))))\n   266\t\n   267\t\n   268\t(defn- observe-subscriptions!\n   269\t  \"Observe every subscription holder's state against this pass's ticks before\n   270\t   anything is projected to it.  A gap on an exchange holder's cursor is a gap\n   271\t   the session reads: every subscription is forgotten and nothing renews.  A\n   272\t   lapsed holder, or one past its bound, drops its subscription.\"\n   273\t  [driver s]\n   274\t  (doseq [[x a] (get-in @driver [:sessions s :subs])]\n   275\t    (lease/step! a)\n   276\t    (cond\n   277\t      (lease/gapped? a) (forget! driver s)\n   278\t      (or (:lapsed? @a) (lease/past-bound? a))\n   279\t      (update-session! driver s (fn [y] (-> y (update :subs dissoc x) (update :sub-staged disj x)))))))\n   280\t\n   281\t\n   282\t(defn- publish!\n   283\t  \"Append the pending transition's fact; only when it answers `ok` does the new\n   284\t   occurrence become the latest and any UI carrying its id get projected.  The\n   285\t   holder's tenure is rechecked first, fail closed: a holder past its bound or\n   286\t   lapsed drops the staged transition (its exchange is left to lapse and the\n   287\t   requester sees silence); a holder not holding for any other reason (a gap)\n   288\t   keeps it staged and publishes nothing.\"\n   289\t  [driver s]\n   290\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   291\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   292\t        {:keys [successor predecessor model exchange halted?]} (:unpublished sess)\n   293\t        agent (:agent sess)]\n   294\t    (when (and sess (:unpublished sess))\n   295\t      (cond\n   296\t        (lease/past-bound? agent)\n   297\t        (update-session! driver s dissoc :unpublished)\n   298\t\n   299\t        (not (lease/holding? agent)) nil\n   300\t\n   301\t        :else\n   302\t        (let [fact (if halted?\n   303\t                     (facts/ended s :halted)\n   304\t                     (facts/consumption s successor predecessor))]\n   305\t          (when (ok? (stream/append! (:facts config) fact))\n   306\t            (update-session! driver s\n   307\t                             (fn [x] (-> x\n   308\t                                         (dissoc :unpublished)\n   309\t                                         (cond-> (not halted?)\n   310\t                                           (assoc :latest {:occurrence successor :model model})))))\n   311\t            (let [occ (if halted? predecessor successor)]\n   312\t              (answer! config exchange occ model)\n   313\t              (when-not halted?\n   314\t                (observe-subscriptions! driver s)\n   315\t                (patch! config (get-in @driver [:sessions s])))\n   316\t              (if halted?\n   317\t                (lease/release! agent)\n   318\t                (lease/renew! agent)))))))))\n   319\t\n   320\t\n   321\t(defn- consume!\n   322\t  \"Step the parked continuation with one input and stage its successor.  Every\n   323\t   consumed input yields a successor, whether or not the program emitted a new\n   324\t   model: when it did not, the previous model is retained.\"\n   325\t  [driver s m]\n   326\t  (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   327\t        input {:signals (signals/decode (:event m))}]\n   328\t    (stream/append! (:vm-in sess) input)\n   329\t    (let [result (await/resume (:result sess))\n   330\t          {:keys [cursor model emitted? gap?]} (last-model (:vm-out sess) (:out-cursor sess))]\n   331\t      (update-session! driver s assoc :result result :out-cursor cursor\n   332\t                       :unpublished {:successor (str (random-uuid))\n   333\t                                     :predecessor (get-in sess [:latest :occurrence])\n   334\t                                     :model (if emitted? model (get-in sess [:latest :model]))\n   335\t                                     :exchange (:exchange m)\n   336\t                                     :halted? (not (:blocked? result))})\n   337\t      (when gap? (forget! driver s))\n   338\t      (publish! driver s))))\n   339\t\n   340\t\n   341\t(defn- subscribe!\n   342\t  \"Open the subscription: its holder starts observing its exchange grant now,\n   343\t   and the head and first projection are staged until the grant is observed.\"\n   344\t  [driver s m]\n   345\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   346\t        x (:exchange m)]\n   347\t    (update-session! driver s\n   348\t                     (fn [sess]\n   349\t                       (-> sess\n   350\t                           (assoc-in [:subs x] (lease/make-agent (exchange-agent-config config x)))\n   351\t                           (update :sub-staged conj x))))))\n   352\t\n   353\t\n   354\t(defn- flush-subscriptions!\n   355\t  \"Project the current occurrence to each staged subscription whose exchange\n   356\t   holder is now holding.\"\n   357\t  [driver s]\n   358\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   359\t        lineage (:agent (get-in @driver [:sessions s]))]\n   360\t    (doseq [x (:sub-staged (get-in @driver [:sessions s]))\n   361\t            :let [a (get-in @driver [:sessions s :subs x])]\n   362\t            :when (and a (lease/holding? a) (lease/holding? lineage))]\n   363\t      (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (get-in @driver [:sessions s :latest])]\n   364\t        (update-session! driver s update :sub-staged disj x)\n   365\t        (emit! config [(head x \"text/event-stream\")\n   366\t                       (chunk-fx x ((:project-fn config) occurrence model))])))))\n   367\t\n   368\t\n   369\t(defn- handle!\n   370\t  \"Handle one routed message.  Answers :wait when the message must stay unread\n   371\t   (no grant observed yet, or the holder is not holding for a reason short of\n   372\t   its bound), :consumed otherwise.  Leased actions are gated on `holding?`,\n   373\t   which fails closed on a missing or invalid reading and on a gap.\"\n   374\t  [driver s m]\n   375\t  (let [{:keys [config]} @driver\n   376\t        sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])\n   377\t        agent (:agent sess)]\n   378\t    (cond\n   379\t      (= :terminal (:kind m))\n   380\t      (do (update-session! driver s (fn [x] (-> x\n   381\t                                                (update :subs dissoc (:exchange m))\n   382\t                                                (update :sub-staged disj (:exchange m)))))\n   383\t          :consumed)\n   384\t\n   385\t      (not (lease/granted? agent)) :wait\n   386\t\n   387\t      (lease/past-bound? agent)\n   388\t      (do (begin! driver (:exchange m)) :consumed)\n   389\t\n   390\t      (not (lease/holding? agent)) :wait\n   391\t\n   392\t      (= :subscribe (:kind m)) (do (subscribe! driver s m) :consumed)\n   393\t\n   394\t      (and (= :input (:kind m))\n   395\t           (= (:token m) (get-in sess [:latest :occurrence])))\n   396\t      (do (consume! driver s m) :consumed)\n   397\t\n   398\t      :else\n   399\t      (let [{:keys [occurrence model]} (:latest sess)]\n   400\t        (answer! config (:exchange m) occurrence model)\n   401\t        :consumed))))\n   402\t\n   403\t\n   404\t(defn- read-messages!\n   405\t  [driver s]\n   406\t  (loop []\n   407\t    (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   408\t      (when (and sess (not (:unpublished sess)))\n   409\t        (let [r (stream/next (:medium sess) (:cursor sess))]\n   410\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   411\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   412\t            (when (= :consumed (handle! driver s (:dao.stream/value r)))\n   413\t              (update-session! driver s assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   414\t              (recur))\n   415\t\n   416\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   417\t            (do (update-session! driver s assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   418\t                (forget! driver s)\n   419\t                (recur))\n   420\t\n   421\t            nil))))))\n   422\t\n   423\t\n   424\t(defn- tick-subscriptions!\n   425\t  \"On the tick: each subscription's holder observes its grant and any lapse,\n   426\t   and renews when due; a lapsed or gapped exchange is dropped.\"\n   427\t  [driver s]\n   428\t  (let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   429\t    (observe-subscriptions! driver s)\n   430\t    (doseq [[_ a] (get-in @driver [:sessions s :subs])]\n   431\t      (lease/renew-if-due! a))\n   432\t    (flush-subscriptions! driver s)\n   433\t    (when (seq (:subs (get-in @driver [:sessions s])))\n   434\t      (lease/renew-if-due! (:agent sess)))))\n   435\t\n   436\t\n   437\t(defn session-step!\n   438\t  [driver s]\n   439\t  (when-let [sess (get-in @driver [:sessions s])]\n   440\t    (let [agent (:agent sess)]\n   441\t      (lease/step! agent)\n   442\t      (when (lease/gapped? agent) (forget! driver s))\n   443\t      (observe-subscriptions! driver s)\n   444\t      (flush-begin! driver s)\n   445\t      (when (lease/release-pending? agent) (lease/release! agent))\n   446\t      (when (:unpublished sess) (publish! driver s))\n   447\t      (read-messages! driver s)\n   448\t      (tick-subscriptions! driver s)))\n   449\t  driver)\n   450\t\n   451\t\n   452\t(defn driver-step!\n   453\t  \"One pass: begin handler, then every session.  Answers the driver.\"\n   454\t  [driver]\n   455\t  (begin-step! driver)\n   456\t  (doseq [s (sessions driver)]\n   457\t    (session-step! driver s))\n   458\t  driver)\n    45\t;; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    46\t\n    47\t(defn make-agent\n    48\t  \"A holder over `lease/make-holder` plus the cursors its control flow drains.\n    49\t   `config` is `make-holder`'s, less the cursors (minted here at the oldest\n    50\t   anchor, so a grant already on the medium is observed).  `:envelope` is merged\n    51\t   into every fact the agent appends (the lineage lease stamps\n    52\t   `:dao.star/lineage` here, which is what the judge's resolver attributes by).\n    53\t   Answers an atom holding the agent state.\"\n    54\t  [{:keys [tick fact writer envelope] :as config}]\n    55\t  (let [wired (lease/make-holder\n    56\t                (assoc config\n    57\t                       :tick {:handle tick :cursor (oldest-cursor tick)}\n    58\t                       :fact {:handle (:handle fact)\n    59\t                              :cursor (oldest-cursor (:handle fact))\n    60\t                              :source (:source fact)\n    61\t                              :medium (:medium fact)}\n    62\t                       :writer writer))]\n    63\t    (atom {:holder (:holder wired)\n    64\t           :tick (:tick wired)\n    65\t           :fact (:fact wired)\n    66\t           :writer (:writer wired)\n    67\t           :envelope (or envelope {})\n    68\t           :reading nil\n    69\t           :pending-facts []\n    70\t           :lapsed? false\n    71\t           :gapped? false\n    72\t           :release nil})))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t(defn- lease-id\n    76\t  [a]\n    77\t  (get-in a [:holder :grant :dao.lease/lease]))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn step!\n    81\t  \"One control-flow pass of the holder: drain its own tick cursor for the\n    82\t   newest reading, then observe its grant (before anything else) and any\n    83\t   `:lapsed` record for its lease.  The fact cursor is read only once a reading\n    84\t   exists: a grant published before the holder's first tick stays unread on the\n    85\t   medium until a reading can observe it.  A `gap` on either cursor marks the\n    86\t   agent `:gapped?`: it renews nothing from then on.  Answers the new state.\"\n    87\t  [agent]\n    88\t  (swap!\n    89\t    agent\n    90\t    (fn [a]\n    91\t      (let [t (drain (get-in a [:tick :handle]) (get-in a [:tick :cursor]))\n    92\t            reading (or (some-> (filter #(= :dao.lease/tick (:dao.lease/event %))\n    93\t                                        (:values t))\n    94\t                                last\n    95\t                                :dao.lease/reading)\n    96\t                        (:reading a))\n    97\t            a (-> a\n    98\t                  (assoc :reading reading)\n    99\t                  (assoc-in [:tick :cursor] (:cursor t))\n   100\t                  (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? t))))]\n   101\t        (if (nil? reading)\n   102\t          a\n   103\t          (let [f (drain (get-in a [:fact :handle]) (get-in a [:fact :cursor]))\n   104\t                retained (:pending-facts a)\n   105\t                a (-> a\n   106\t                      (assoc-in [:fact :cursor] (:cursor f))\n   107\t                      (assoc :pending-facts [])\n   108\t                      (update :gapped? #(or % (:gap? f))))]\n   109\t            (reduce\n   110\t              (fn [a v]\n   111\t                (cond\n   112\t                  (nil? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   113\t                  (let [a (update a :holder lease/observe-grant (get-in a [:fact :source]) v reading)]\n   114\t                    ;; A grant a reading could not yet observe (an unusable\n   115\t                    ;; reading) is retained and retried, never discarded.\n   116\t                    (if (and (nil? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   117\t                             (= :dao.lease/accepted (:dao.lease/status v)))\n   118\t                      (update a :pending-facts conj v)\n   119\t                      a))\n   120\t\n   121\t                  (and (= :dao.lease/lapsed (:dao.lease/status v))\n   122\t                       (some? (lease-id a))\n   123\t                       (= (lease-id a) (:dao.lease/lease v)))\n   124\t                  (assoc a :lapsed? true)\n   125\t\n   126\t                  :else a))\n   127\t              a\n   128\t              (concat retained (:values f)))))))))\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t(defn gapped?\n   132\t  \"True once any cursor the agent reads answered `gap`.\"\n   133\t  [agent]\n   134\t  (boolean (:gapped? @agent)))\n   135\t\n   136\t\n   137\t(defn release-pending?\n   138\t  \"True while a release fact is staged and not yet appended with `ok`.\"\n   139\t  [agent]\n   140\t  (some? (:release @agent)))\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t(defn holding?\n   144\t  \"May the control flow act: a grant observed, not stopped, not at its bound,\n   145\t   not lapsed, and no gap seen.\"\n   146\t  [agent]\n   147\t  (let [a @agent]\n   148\t    (boolean (and (not (:lapsed? a))\n   149\t                  (not (:gapped? a))\n   150\t                  (some? (:reading a))\n   151\t                  (lease/holding? (:holder a) (:reading a))))))\n   152\t\n   153\t\n   154\t(defn granted?\n   155\t  [agent]\n   156\t  (some? (get-in @agent [:holder :grant])))\n   157\t\n   158\t\n   159\t(defn past-bound?\n   160\t  \"True once the agent has left the lease for good: it lapsed, was released,\n   161\t   or reached its bound.  A gap is not that: the agent renews nothing after one\n   162\t   but the lease is not known to be over.\"\n   163\t  [agent]\n   164\t  (let [a @agent]\n   165\t    (boolean (or (:lapsed? a)\n   166\t                 (get-in a [:holder :released?])\n   167\t                 (get-in a [:holder :bound-reached?])\n   168\t                 (and (some? (:reading a)) (some? (get-in a [:holder :grant]))\n   169\t                      (lease/at-bound? (:holder a) (:reading a)))))))\n   170\t\n   171\t\n   172\t(defn- append-renewal!\n   173\t  [agent]\n   174\t  (let [a @agent\n   175\t        fact (merge (lease/renewal (lease-id a)) (:envelope a))\n     1\t(ns dao.star.signals\n     2\t  \"Decode a request's client signals from an `:http/request` event\n     3\t   (docs/design/dao.star.md, Signals).\n     4\t\n     5\t   Signals are the client's unverified claim, so on the JVM and ClojureScript\n     6\t   `decode` is total: a missing, malformed or non-map input answers `{}` and\n     7\t   nothing throws.  (The one exception is the ClojureDart seam, below.)  GET and DELETE\n     8\t   carry them in the query parameter the spec names, every other method in the\n     9\t   JSON body.  The JSON parse is the host's; a host without one decodes\n    10\t   nothing.\n    11\t\n    12\t   Scope: the JSON and URL-decoding seams are implemented for the JVM and\n    13\t   ClojureScript only.  On ClojureDart they are unimplemented, and `decode`\n    14\t   throws `ex-info` naming the seam (`:dao.star.signals/seam`) rather than\n    15\t   answer `{}`, which would be indistinguishable from absent signals.\"\n    16\t  (:require [clojure.string :as str]\n    17\t            [dao.host.bytes :as bytes]\n    18\t            [dao.host.text :as text]\n    19\t            #?(:clj [clojure.data.json :as json])))\n    20\t\n    21\t\n    22\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unused-private-var]}\n    23\t(defn- unimplemented\n    24\t  [seam]\n31:(deftest an-input-triggered-patch-needs-the-exchange-holder-in-tenure\n51:(deftest a-staged-subscription-is-not-projected-after-the-lineage-bound\n69:(deftest an-exchange-holder-gap-cleans-the-whole-session\n94:(deftest an-unusable-first-reading-does-not-discard-the-grant\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/dao/star/r4_test.clj; sed -n '1739,1789p' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; sed -n '88,101p' docs/design/dao.star.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/dao/star/r4_test.clj; sed -n '1739,1789p' src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc; sed -n '88,101p' docs/design/dao.star.md\"","aggregated_output":"(ns dao.star.r4-test\n  \"Round r4: tenure enforced on every projection path, a gap on any exchange\n   holder cleaning the whole session, and grants retained until a usable\n   reading can observe them.  Holder ticks and judge ticks are scheduled\n   independently.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.lease :as dl]\n            [dao.star.driver :as driver]\n            [dao.star.driver-test :as h]\n            [dao.star.lease :as lease]\n            [dao.star.router :as router]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]))\n\n\n(defn- driver-tick!\n  \"Move only the driver's tick stream: the holders' clock, not the judges'.\"\n  [w ms]\n  (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks :driver]) (dl/tick {:ms ms})))\n\n\n(defn- chunks\n  [w x]\n  (count (filter #(= :http/chunk (:http/effect %)) (h/effects w x))))\n\n\n(defn- renewals\n  [w]\n  (count (filter #(= :dao.lease/renewal (:dao.lease/event %)) (h/values (:egress w)))))\n\n\n(deftest an-input-triggered-patch-needs-the-exchange-holder-in-tenure\n  (let [w (h/start! (h/world {:duration-ms 100 :subscription-max-ms 200}))\n        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n        sub (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))]\n    (h/pump! w)\n    (dotimes [_ 17] (h/advance! w 10))\n    (is (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub) \"live below its cap\")\n    (let [before (chunks w sub)]\n      ;; the driver's clock alone reaches the exchange cap; the lineage, renewed\n      ;; a moment ago, is still live\n      (driver-tick! w 240)\n      (let [x (h/call! w :post (str \"/k/\" s) \"{}\")]\n        (router/router-step! (:router w))\n        (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n        (is (= 1 (count (h/consumption-facts w))) \"the input was consumed: the lineage is live\")\n        (is (seq (h/effects w x)) \"and answered\")\n        (is (= before (chunks w sub)) \"but no patch reached the subscription past its cap\")\n        (is (not (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub)))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-staged-subscription-is-not-projected-after-the-lineage-bound\n  (let [w (h/start! (h/world {:duration-ms 100}))\n        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n        sub (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))]\n    ;; router and driver only: the subscription is staged, its exchange grant\n    ;; has not been published\n    (router/router-step! (:router w))\n    (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n    (is (contains? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s) sub))\n    ;; the driver's clock passes the lineage bound, then the exchange grant lands\n    (driver-tick! w 210)\n    (lease/exchange-lease-step! (:xl w))\n    (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n    (is (lease/granted? (get-in @(:driver w) [:sessions s :subs sub]))\n        \"the exchange holder has observed its grant and is holding\")\n    (is (empty? (h/effects w sub)) \"yet nothing is projected: the lineage is past its bound\")))\n\n\n(deftest an-exchange-holder-gap-cleans-the-whole-session\n  (let [w (h/start! (h/world {:duration-ms 1000}))\n        s (h/begin-lineage! w)\n        sub1 (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))\n        _ (h/pump! w)\n        sub2 (h/call! w :get (str \"/s/\" s))\n        _ (h/pump! w)\n        agent-of #(get-in @(:driver w) [:sessions s :subs %])\n        flood! #(dotimes [_ 40] (stream/append! (:exchange-lease w) {:junk 1}))]\n    (dotimes [_ 40] (h/advance! w 10))\n    (is (pos? (renewals w)))\n    (is (= #{sub1 sub2} (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s)))\n    (flood!)\n    (lease/step! (agent-of sub2))             ; sub2's cursor moves up, sub1's does not\n    (flood!)\n    (lease/step! (agent-of sub2))\n    (is (not (lease/gapped? (agent-of sub2))) \"the sibling's cursor is newer and clean\")\n    (driver/driver-step! (:driver w))\n    (is (empty? (driver/subscriptions (:driver w) s)) \"the gap cleans every subscription\")\n    (is (lease/gapped? (driver/lineage-agent (:driver w) s)) \"and the lineage renews nothing\")\n    (let [before (renewals w)]\n      (dotimes [_ 10] (h/advance! w 10))\n      (is (= before (renewals w))))))\n\n\n(deftest an-unusable-first-reading-does-not-discard-the-grant\n  (let [w (h/world)]\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks :exchange]) (dl/tick {:ms 10}))\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks :lineage]) (dl/tick {:ms 10}))\n    ;; the holder's first reading is not a usable duration\n    (stream/append! (get-in w [:ticks :driver])\n                    {:dao.lease/event :dao.lease/tick :dao.lease/reading {:ms 0}})\n    (let [x (h/call! w :get \"/\")]\n      (h/pump! w)\n      (let [s (first (driver/sessions (:driver w)))\n            agent (driver/lineage-agent (:driver w) s)]\n        (is (some #(= :dao.lease/accepted (:dao.lease/status %)) (h/values (:lineage-lease w))))\n        (is (not (lease/granted? agent)) \"an unusable reading observes nothing\")\n        (is (empty? (h/effects w x)))\n        (testing \"a usable reading later observes the retained grant, and the holder proceeds\"\n          (driver-tick! w 10)\n          (h/pump! w)\n          (is (lease/granted? agent))\n          (is (= [:http/head :http/chunk :http/end] (mapv :http/effect (h/effects w x)))))))))\n(defn observe-grant\n  \"H1: observe the grant before acting. The grant is held only when the\n  fact is a structurally valid `:accepted` naming this holder\n  (`:dao.lease/holder` = `:self`) whose author, by the composition's\n  resolver bound to the source the fact was read from, is the grantor --\n  the same attribution seam the judge resolves with -- and, when the\n  state carries a `:subject` or `:proposal` expectation (wired at\n  assembly by a holder that proposed), the grant's subject and answered\n  proposal match it; a grant answering no proposal matches no proposal\n  expectation. Anything else -- a forged or non-grantor `:accepted`, a\n  grant naming another holder or another lease's proposal, a\n  structurally defective fact, a refusal -- establishes nothing: the\n  holder is returned unchanged and `:grant` nil is the report \\\"no grant\n  observed\\\"; a holder with `:grant` nil holds nothing, and every\n  discipline below answers false.\n\n  `reading` is the newest reading drained from the holder's OWN tick\n  cursor at the moment of observation -- the tenure basis no renewal\n  moves, which the cap binds -- and no clock supplies it. A reading that\n  is not a well-shaped, in-table, in-bound duration observes nothing\n  (mirroring the judge's first-tick rule; see `reading-ok?`).\n\n  Sizing is checked where the interval and the GRANTED duration are known\n  together, because the grantor may grant shorter than the ask: an\n  undersized grant -- interval + interval not strictly below the granted\n  duration, equality included -- is still HELD, recorded `:undersized?`:\n  the holder holds what it was granted, the grantor's word, and may\n  release it, but every discipline function treats it as at the bound --\n  no renewal is due, no renewal advances anything, `holding?` is false.\n\n  The first observed grant is the one held: observation seeds the basis\n  once, and no later fact moves it (a fresh lease id is a different\n  lease; a holder holding several threads one state per lease). A\n  resolver that throws propagates the throw: attribution failure is loud,\n  and the control flow observing through a broken seam observes nothing.\"\n  [holder source fact reading]\n  (if (and (reading-ok? holder reading)\n           (lease-fact? fact)\n           (= :dao.lease/accepted (get fact status-key))\n           (not (defective? fact (:units holder)))\n           (= (:self holder) (get fact :dao.lease/holder))\n           (= (:grantor holder) ((:resolver holder) source fact))\n           (nil? (:grant holder))\n           (or (nil? (:subject holder))\n               (= (:subject holder) (get fact :dao.lease/subject)))\n           (or (nil? (:proposal holder))\n               (= (:proposal holder) (get fact :dao.lease/proposal))))\n    (assoc holder\n           :grant fact\n           :granted-at reading\n           :last-renewal-at nil\n### Liveness\n\nTwo leased resources, kept apart. Neither adds a clock to the wait for input: a parked continuation's `next` on its input is `blocked` until a request arrives, on a Tuesday or a Thursday.\n\n**The open exchange is leased.** The judge runs inside the peer that holds the HTTP boundary and is composed with the boundary's `close-exchange` as reclaim procedure and `open-exchanges` as its inventory (`dao.stream.http.md`, Inventory). For each `:http/request` it observes it grants unsolicited on a lease medium it writes: subject `{:http/exchange x}`, holder the egress medium's identity, a duration in `{:ms 1 :s 1000}`, and a `:dao.lease/max` cap that subscription exchanges are required to carry, so no subscription is uncapped (architect ruling 2026-10-24, `collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2`). Reclaim closes the exchange; the adapter deposits `:http/closed`, then the judge records `:lapsed`. A responder that keeps an exchange open observes its grant and appends `{:dao.lease/event :dao.lease/renewal :dao.lease/lease L}` to the egress medium at under half the duration, from its own control flow, against its own tick stream. The judge and `egress-step` are peer observers of that medium; each ignores the other's facts. A one-shot responder answers inside the granted duration and renews nothing. An exchange nobody answers lapses by `:silence`; Datastar's reconnect opens a new one.\n\n**A gap is loss, and nothing is forwarded about it.** The judge, on an ingress `gap`, reconciles both ways against the inventory: an open exchange without a lease is granted afresh, and a leased exchange absent from the inventory is recorded `:lapsed` with cause `:policy`, so nothing is held unleased and nothing closed stays leased (inventory reconciliation; `dao.lease.md`'s reclaim-and-regrant is reserved for a lost ledger). The router forwards nothing about a gap: a request or terminal event lost in the evicted window is unrouted, and a forward whose `append!` answers anything but `ok` is the same loss; an unrouted request's exchange lapses by `:silence`. Drivers learn that an exchange is gone from the lease medium they already read for their grants: a `:lapsed` record for one of their exchanges drops it (`dao.lease.md`, Carriage). A driver whose cursor on any medium it reads answers `gap` forgets every subscription it holds and renews none; they lapse by `:silence` and close, and Datastar's reconnect subscribes again. Session media are declared at assembly like any deposit destination, evict-oldest with a capacity, and sized against the driver's lag.\n\n**Keep-alive is the responder's.** On its tick it may append an `:http/chunk` carrying an SSE comment line. That chunk is bytes for the wire, so a host that reports write failure discovers a dead peer by writing; the renewal is evidence for the judge. Neither stands in for the other. A peer's close or a reported write failure is deposited as `:http/closed`; the responder reads it as data and drops the exchange, and the judge ends the exchange lease with cause `:policy`. A host whose send buffers and whose close notification is silent for an idle exchange (http-kit is one) reports neither, so a chunk written to a dead peer is not evidence of anything, and a responder that keeps renewing a subscription it believes open keeps the lease alive. Such an exchange ends at its lease's `:dao.lease/max`, not before (architect ruling 2026-10-24, `collab/1792841840885-architect-dao-star-m1-reconcile-r2`).\n\n**The lineage is leased** (owner ruling 2026-10-07; the holder choice below is the architect's). A lineage nobody returns to is reclaimed through `dao.lease.md`, not by a timer. The peer holding the parked record is the grantor. When a lineage begins, its judge grants unsolicited on the lease medium: subject and holder `{:dao.star/lineage S}`, duration the composition's idle allowance, `:dao.lease/max` optional. Attribution is by envelope key: the session-facts medium is written only by session drivers, each stamping `:dao.star/lineage` on its facts, renewals and release, and the judge's resolver reads that key; until ShiBi, any writer of that medium can renew, the same exposure the exchange lease has. The driver observes its grant before consuming or projecting, renews at under half the duration from its own control flow, on each consumed input and on its tick while it holds an open subscription, and **stops at its bound**: past it, it consumes nothing and projects nothing, and an input arriving then is handed to the root program as begin. So a connected session is retained for as long as it stays connected, by design, bounded only by the cap; a disconnected one lapses after the idle allowance. The lease ends with the lineage: released by the driver on halt, lapsed by the judge on silence. Reclaim retires the runnable resource, the current parked record; the `:lapsed` record on the lease medium is the judge's own and is what ends the lineage for the router. History, successor facts and lease records are kept (`dao.lease.md`: a reclaim frees the resource, never the record). The subject is distinct from Mode 2's custody subject `{:yin.k/occurrence O}` on the arbitration medium. Leases are process-scoped until the composition settles the three durable duties `dao.lease.md` names.\n\nSizing: duration exceeds twice the renewal interval; the keep-alive interval stays under the shortest proxy or NAT idle timeout on the path; the ingress window exceeds router and judge lag and each session medium's window exceeds its driver's; a boundary restart loses sockets and ledger together, so its exchange inventory to reclaim is empty. The duration bounds silence, not death. The detection bound for a peer that disconnects while an exchange is idle is the exchange lease's `:dao.lease/max` on a host that does not report the close, and the host's own close notification, when it gives one, on a host that does. The composition sizes `:dao.lease/max` against the longest it will tolerate a dead subscription holding a socket and a driver slot, and accepts that every healthy subscription reconnects at that interval. A false lapse is possible (`dao.lease.md`, Limits).\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-24 13:05:46 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-24 20:05:46 +07\n\nStatic review only; no edits or suite reruns.\n\n- **Gap 1 — resolved:** `src/cljc/dao/star/driver.cljc:443` observes subscription holders before processing inputs; `:314` refreshes them before patches; `:145` checks exchange tenure; `:362` checks both lineage and exchange tenure before staged projection. The two independently scheduled tests exercise the previously missing cases.\n- **Gap 2 — resolved:** `driver.cljc:277` invokes session-wide `forget!`, clearing subscriptions and marking the lineage gapped (`:199`). Subsequent renewal iterates the updated subscription set (`:430`). The two-cursor test covers sibling cleanup.\n- **Gap 3 — partially resolved:** `src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc:104–128` preserves rejected grants across unusable readings, but loses associated lapse records. This introduces the defect below.\n- **Docstring — resolved:** `src/cljc/dao/star/signals.cljc:5` now qualifies totality by supported host and identifies the CLJD exception.\n\n**HIGH | `src/cljc/dao/star/lease.cljc:112` | Deferred grants can outlive an observed lapse.**\n\nWhile ungranted, every value takes the first conditional branch. With an unusable reading:\n\n1. An `:accepted` grant is retained in `:pending-facts`.\n2. A following `:lapsed` for that lease is discarded: `observe-grant` rejects it, and only accepted facts are retained.\n3. On a later usable reading, the retained grant establishes tenure. The lapse is already behind the advanced cursor.\n\nThe holder can then report holding, renew, or permit staged projection despite having read its lease’s retirement. The new invalid-reading test covers only a grant followed by recovery, so it misses this interaction.\n\n**Recommended correction:** defer fact-cursor advancement until a usable reading exists, or preserve ordered lifecycle evidence—including lapses—alongside deferred grants. Add a grant → lapse → usable-reading test asserting no tenure, renewal, or projection.\n\nThe flagged **foreign-grant residual** does not grant authority to the wrong holder: `observe-grant` still checks attribution and addressing. However, pending storage can grow indefinitely if the holder’s own grant never arrives. Filtering permanently inapplicable grants would avoid that resource risk; distinguish them from applicable grants deferred solely because of an unusable reading.\n\nThe projection and gap fixes appear complete for the reviewed paths. The deferred-grant lifecycle defect blocks sign-off.\n\n**NOT SIGNED OFF**"}}
